        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1708,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-06T03:15:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Look the code again, I think we don\u0027t need to check whether listener is already registered.\nHere is reason:\n1. We already check whether listener is registered in ConnectivityManager.\n2. If binder died(process of app is down), the callback would be removed from mTetheringEventListeners automatically.\n3. throw exception would crash the system, I don\u0027t think it is a good idea to crash system only for duplicated callback register. User should response for not registered duplicated callback.",
      "parentUuid": "f8b99a43_13bf7e1c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1708,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1708,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a77e0cd61eafa73e0e1e72180fc5c37be43639d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47fdb1da_34e0e231",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1708,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-06T10:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do it in ConnectivityManager, but apps may bypass that.\n\nThis is a binder thread right ? The call is coming from an external app. If you throw an exception here, you crash the app, not the system. That\u0027s what happens in the caller for this method : ConnectivityService#registerTetheringEventListener throws SecurityException if the caller app does not have the correct permissions.",
      "parentUuid": "f1feb052_d07a4aff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1708,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1708,
        "endChar": 15
      },
