      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T07:45:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Catching RuntimeException is a code smell. In this case I suspect you are doing this to catch the possible OOB and NPE from removing while iterating, but you also need to account for the add case. Also if you have a call to remove while iterating, you will miss calling one of the callbacks : if e.g. you have four callbacks in the list\n(A, B, C, D)\n\nIterate, call index 1 \u003d A\nIterate, call index 2 \u003d B\nRemove index 1\nIterate, call index 3 \u003d D\nIterate, call index 4, NPE, catch RuntimeException\n\n...you never called C.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1730,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 1730,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "a77e0cd61eafa73e0e1e72180fc5c37be43639d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
